tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance", "lar:///carriage.bag.reads"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.bag.reads"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.bag.reads"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.bag.reads ~ what a bag declares: its tier, its home, and whether it sits where it belongs

With no bag, `show` surveys every bag the survey dir holds: its declared cap-tier and home, and whether it sits where its declaration says. With a bag, it shows that bag's declaration and where it resolves ON THIS VESSEL: tier (a tier only ever tightens against the structural floor), home (and the repo it names), whether a clone of the repo carries it, where its bytes sit, and where it declares they belong, with an ADRIFT mark and the command that re-anchors it where the two differ.

The survey reads `dir=` (default the bags dir); with no `dir=`, a bag with no canon source resolves in the house's projected bags, and a shared wiki's canon bag under its realm folder. A bag absent from every place names each place it read. `after=` and `limit=` page the whole survey; naming one bag takes `dir=` alone.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ survey · one-bag · a-page

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`survey` params=`~ every bag, its declared tier and home`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`one-bag` params=`bag/lares ~ one bag's declaration and its resolution here`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-page` params=`limit/10 after/<cursor> ~ ten rows behind a cursor an answer named`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ bag · dir · limit · after

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/slug seat/1 as/<bag> ~ one bag; absent, the whole survey`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`dir` params=`takes/dir ~ where the bags are looked for; default the bags dir`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`limit` params=`takes/count ~ rows per page of the survey`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`after` params=`takes/cursor ~ the page behind a cursor an answer named`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ read

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`read` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ a local read of the bags and their declarations; it writes nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ bag-absent

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`bag-absent` params=`cure/[[carriage.bag.reads]] ~ no place the survey read holds the bag; the line names each place it read`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ survey · declaration

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`survey` params=`exit/0 ~ each bag with its declared tier and home, and whether it sits where it belongs`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`declaration` params=`exit/0 fields/[[bag manifest dir adrift]] ~ one bag's declaration and where it resolves here`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

